<title>CANADA: Goodale names new chief of Canada Grain Commission.</title>
<headline>Goodale names new chief of Canada Grain Commission.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Agriculture Minister Ralph Goodale on Monday named a new chief commissioner of the Canadian Grain Commission.</p>
<p>Barry Senft, of Regina, Saskatchewan, succeeds Milt Wakefield at the head of the grain and oilseed grading and regulating agency, an Agriculture Canada statement said.</p>
<p>Senft was assistant chief commission of the CGC since January. Douglas Stow, of Carman, Manitoba, replaces Senft as assistant chief commissioner, it said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
